{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.KZ.KZShift","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.KZ.KZShift","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.PowerSeries.Basic"],"declarations":26,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZShift.phiKZ_shift_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZShift.phiKZ_shift_left","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZShift.lean#L259-L276","doc":"**Shift invariance at `0`.** If `z` commutes with `A`, `B` and the formal solutions, then\n`Φ_KZ(A + z, B) = Φ_KZ(A, B)` (from `phiKZ_shift_right` and the inversion relation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZShift.phiKZ_shift_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZShift.phiKZ_shift_right","kind":"theorem","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZShift.lean#L225-L257","doc":"**Shift invariance at `1`.** If `z` commutes with `A`, `B` and the formal solutions, then\n`Φ_KZ(A, B + z) = Φ_KZ(A, B)`. The normalised solution at `0` of the shifted system is the Cauchy\nproduct of `H₀` with the binomial series `E = (1 − t)^z`; the one at `1` is `H₁` itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZShift.commute_phiKZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZShift.commute_phiKZ","kind":"theorem","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZShift.lean#L205-L223","doc":"`Φ_KZ(A, B)` commutes with every `c` commuting with `A`, `B` and the formal solutions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZShift.commute_tpow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZShift.commute_tpow","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZShift.lean#L202-L203","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZShift.commute_series","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZShift.commute_series","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZShift.lean#L197-L199","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZShift.isFormalGauge_kzM0_add_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZShift.isFormalGauge_kzM0_add_left","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZShift.lean#L184-L194","doc":"If `z` commutes with every `H_k`, then `H` solves `kzM0 (B + z) A` iff it solves `kzM0 B A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZShift.series_conv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZShift.series_conv","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZShift.lean#L171-L181","doc":"The Cauchy product of convergent series. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZShift.conv_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZShift.conv_zero","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZShift.lean#L168-L169","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZShift.series_eq_tpow_one_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZShift.series_eq_tpow_one_sub","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZShift.lean#L141-L165","doc":"**The binomial series.** If `E` is the normalised formal solution of `kzM0 0 z` (so\n`k E_k = −z ∑_{j<k} E_j`), then `∑ t^k E_k = (1 − t)^z` on `(0, 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZShift.tpow_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZShift.tpow_one","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZShift.lean#L138-L139","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZShift.tpow_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZShift.tpow_zero","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZShift.lean#L134-L135","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZShift.isFormalGauge_delta0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZShift.isFormalGauge_delta0","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZShift.lean#L128-L131","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZShift.series_delta0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZShift.series_delta0","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZShift.lean#L122-L125","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZShift.delta0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZShift.delta0","kind":"def","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZShift.lean#L118-L119","doc":"The coefficient sequence `1, 0, 0, …`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZShift.isFormalGauge_conv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZShift.isFormalGauge_conv","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZShift.lean#L89-L108","doc":"**Formal shift.** If `H` solves `kzM0 A B` and `E` solves `kzM0 0 z` (so `E = (1 − w)^z`),\nwith `z` commuting with every `H_k` and every `E_k` commuting with `A`, then the Cauchy product\n`H E` solves `kzM0 A (B + z)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZShift.ser_kzM0_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZShift.ser_kzM0_add","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZShift.lean#L85-L87","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZShift.ser_conv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZShift.ser_conv","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZShift.lean#L82-L83","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZShift.conv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZShift.conv","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZShift.lean#L79-L80","doc":"The Cauchy product of coefficient sequences. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZShift.ser_mul_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZShift.ser_mul_comm","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZShift.lean#L70-L77","doc":"Series whose coefficients commute pairwise commute. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZShift.isFormalGauge_iff_euler","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZShift.isFormalGauge_iff_euler","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZShift.lean#L64-L68","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZShift.coeff_ser_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZShift.coeff_ser_mul","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZShift.lean#L58-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZShift.coeff_gaugeLHS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZShift.coeff_gaugeLHS","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZShift.lean#L54-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZShift.ser","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZShift.ser","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZShift.lean#L51-L52","doc":"The power series with coefficient sequence `H`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZShift.euler_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZShift.euler_mul","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZShift.lean#L40-L49","doc":"`Θ` is a derivation (no commutativity needed: the integer `k` is central). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZShift.coeff_euler","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZShift.coeff_euler","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZShift.lean#L37-L38","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZShift.euler","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZShift.euler","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZShift.lean#L34-L35","doc":"The Euler operator `Θ = w d/dw` on power series. ","signatureChunk":0}]}